content.text:
Yes—the previous helper was still too item-specific.

I generalized it to `resolveIconReference(record, defaultAtlas)`:

- corpses use explicit `iconAtlas: "corpses"`;
- spells use `"spells"`;
- statuses use `"statuses"`;
- ordinary items default to `"items"`;
- future atlases work by adding a manifest/registry entry and metadata;
- unidentified records still suppress their icon ID.

All current UI icon surfaces now route through that resolver. The room remains ASCII/Unicode-only.

Verification: 9 focused tests passed, plus `deno check` and `git diff --check`.

